                <pb facs="0707" n="627" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg627"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Powell reports that the <hi rendition="#italic">D’Assas</hi> has returned;
                    brings news that Petit Goave is entirely destroyed; 10,000 people homeless;
                    foreigners at coffee usine; the <hi rendition="#italic">D’Assas</hi> brought 150
                    women and children to Port au Prince; that Killick blockades Cape, refusing the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Paloma</hi> entrance on August 10.</p>
                <p>Mr. Powell has instructed Consul Livingston to ignore the blockade.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
